# Normalize line endings.
#
# The repo had no .gitattributes and `core.autocrlf` was false, so git performed
# no conversion at all. That let the tree drift into a genuinely mixed state --
# `LeftDock.tsx` and `AskPanel.tsx` were CRLF while the other ~140 tracked files
# were LF -- and any tool that wrote CRLF produced a whole-file rewrite in
# `git diff` instead of a one-line change. The phantom diffs were pure noise and
# had to be chased down more than once.
#
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect binary content so images stay untouched, and
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF on every platform. LF is already the
# majority convention here and is what the Node/Vite toolchain expects.
* text=auto eol=lf

